.TH ag-init 1  "init 0.3.0-beta.3"
.SH NAME
ag\-init \- Create a repository in the current directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag init\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-namespace\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-stream\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-storage\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-preset\fR] [\fB\-\-admin\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-issuer\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-ci\-key\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a repository in the current directory
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-namespace\fR \fI<NAMESPACE>\fR
Repository namespace, e.g. `acme/webapp` (default: `local/<directory name>`)
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR \fI<STREAM>\fR [default: main]
Name of the first stream
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-storage\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
JSON file with the `storage` section (PostgreSQL metadata and/or S3 objects); see docs/operations/postgres\-and\-s3.md. Default: a SQLite file and local objects under `.ag/`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-\-preset\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Store a ready\-made policy for the first stream: solo, team, agents or strict (`ag policy preset list`)
.TP
\fB\-\-admin\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Identity pattern allowed to change the policy (repeatable). Default: you
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-\-issuer\fR \fI<IDENTITY=KEY>\fR
Trust this CI issuer to sign the `tests` check: IDENTITY=PUBLIC_KEY, e.g. service:ci=<64 hex digits>
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-\-ci\-key\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Trust the signing key NAME of this repository (created if missing; `ag validate keygen NAME` makes the same key): the issuer becomes service:NAME
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0\-beta.3
